<heading>go - Move to another box.</heading>
<rule/>
<heading level="2">Usage</heading>
<pre>go DIRECTION
go NAME
go ..</pre>
<heading level="2">Description</heading>
<paragraph>Moves to a connected box via an exit or to a child box. The target is matched by endpoint name first, then by orientation (compass word or angle).</paragraph>
<paragraph>Use go .. to move back to the parent box. Following a connection that leads into another world moves you into that world.</paragraph>
<heading level="2">Examples</heading>
<pre>go north
  Follow an endpoint leading north.
go Kitchen
  Move to a box or endpoint called Kitchen.
go ..
  Move back to the parent box.</pre>
<heading level="2">See also</heading>
<paragraph>dig, enter, leave, look, refine split</paragraph>
